00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.781
Let's dive in to this
story about supplements.

00:03:57.781 --> 00:04:00.198
(drum bangs)

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:03.060
It's easy to look at stuff like this,

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.400
and say it's kind of like medicine,

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.520
and so it would be kind of
regulated like medicine,

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.700
tracked and vetted by our
government's health agency

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:12.630
like medicine is.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:15.090
But medicine goes through
a very different process,

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:18.060
a super lengthy process
with tons of studies

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.610
and clinical trials, paperwork.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.200
It takes years and years,

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.140
and a lot of drugs aren't
ever even approved.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.430
They fail this process,

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.140
and never make it onto the shelf.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.971
But supplements don't
have to do any of that.

00:04:30.971 --> 00:04:33.210
- Companies are responsible for ensuring

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.440
their products are safe,

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.366
and in fact can often

00:04:35.366 --> 00:04:37.950
put new dietary supplements on the market

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.960
without even telling FDA.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.210
- There are rules on
what supplement companies

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.910
are allowed to put in
their pills and gummies,

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.730
but these rules aren't
enforced in any real way.

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.220
It's up to the supplement
company to obey them.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.142
- With dietary supplements
it's on the honor system

00:04:53.142 --> 00:04:56.400
that they are following
those rules and regulations.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.350
- That's Dr. C. Michael White,

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.360
- A pharmacist, distinguished professor

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.890
and chair of pharmacy practice

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:03.959
at the University of
Connecticut School of Pharmacy.

00:05:03.959 --> 00:05:06.480
- And this is Dr. F. Perry Wilson.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.061
- I am a physician and researcher
here at Yale University.

00:05:10.061 --> 00:05:10.950
(bell dings)

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.500
- These two doctors helped
us a lot in our reporting,

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.020
helped us navigate this
really complex topic,

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.400
and helped us better understand

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.250
how this $50 billion a year industry

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:23.070
runs wild with all of these products

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.510
that make health claims

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.853
that are often not backed up by anything.

00:05:28.196 --> 00:05:30.897
There's a wild story on how we got here,

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:32.953
and to understand it we
have to go back to the 80's

00:05:32.953 --> 00:05:36.180
and 90's to understand
this political commercial

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.210
featuring Mel Gibson
and health supplements.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.260
- It's only vitamins.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.830
- [Reporter] Nelson Mandela
got a rousing welcome

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.120
from the city of New York today.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.500
- The East German authorities have said

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.570
the Berlin Wall doesn't
mean anything anymore.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.710
- Oh yeah.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:52.434
- The 90's was a time of
economic prosperity in America,

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:53.613
which fueled the rise

00:05:53.613 --> 00:05:56.250
of a health conscious middle class

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.328
that was increasingly
attracted to health foods

00:05:58.328 --> 00:05:59.880
and fitness regimes,

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.410
and alternative medicine.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:02.280
- I avoid sugar,

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.683
that makes me feel good about me.

00:06:03.683 --> 00:06:05.400
- To cater to this shift,

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.170
you have this supplement industry,

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.360
which was very small
and niche at the time,

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.085
but they met the demand
of this new middle class

00:06:12.085 --> 00:06:14.400
and began diversifying their offerings.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.400
They expanded beyond the
typical vitamin C tablets

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.690
and echinacea drops,

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.804
introducing a variety of new substances,

00:06:20.804 --> 00:06:24.553
each purporting to enhance
one's life in unique ways.

00:06:24.553 --> 00:06:27.171
One of the supplements
that gained popularity

00:06:27.171 --> 00:06:29.043
was called L-Tryptophan.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.890
It was this health food supplement

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.170
made of amino acids that claimed to

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:36.270
help people sleep and lose weight.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.010
It sounded healthy enough

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.241
until doctors found that
people who took the stuff

00:06:40.241 --> 00:06:41.475
were developing blood

00:06:41.475 --> 00:06:43.110
and muscle disorders.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:46.530
Investigations found that it
led to the death of 38 people.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.188
In response to this incident,

00:06:48.188 --> 00:06:49.794
Congress began drafting laws

00:06:49.794 --> 00:06:52.860
that would tighten regulation
on health supplements.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.025
So they drafted this bill.

00:06:54.025 --> 00:06:57.240
The bill would give more power to the FDA

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:58.890
to regulate these companies,

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.960
to tighten the rules on how supplements

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.340
were able to be labeled,

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:03.960
what claims they could make.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.400
But, as we know,

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.900
whenever there's a growing industry

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.060
that's making a lot of
money off of selling things

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.399
and the government comes in
and tries to regulate them,

00:07:11.399 --> 00:07:13.950
they don't just sit
back and let it happen.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.870
So all the supplement
companies got together,

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.400
they held these emergency meetings,

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.207
they sent an army of
lobbyists to Washington,

00:07:19.207 --> 00:07:22.507
and they started pouring
money on commercials.

00:07:22.507 --> 00:07:23.754
- Help make sure your child

00:07:23.754 --> 00:07:26.370
gets a balanced diet with Flintstones.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.750
- And this is where Mel Gibson,

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:30.622
the 90's movie star, comes into the story.

00:07:30.622 --> 00:07:33.205
(gentle music)

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:35.280
- [Officer] Freeze.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.230
- Hey guys, guys, it's
got it's only vitamins.

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.659
Vitamin C, you know, like in oranges.

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:41.970
- [Narrator] If you don't
wanna lose your vitamins,

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.415
make the FDA stop.

00:07:43.415 --> 00:07:45.540
- Yeah, they weren't messing around here.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.770
They published books,

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.110
they sent flyers to people's mailboxes.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.490
They produced more commercials,

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.130
they created petitions to rally Americans

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:55.200
around their supplements,

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.370
and it worked.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.890
More and more Americans
were taking supplements,

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:00.510
and they responded to

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:02.757
this potential tightening of regulation,

00:08:02.757 --> 00:08:04.807
and all of this fear
mongering by the lobbyists

00:08:04.807 --> 00:08:06.542
by writing to Congress,

00:08:06.542 --> 00:08:09.450
telling the government not
to regulate supplements,

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.430
to let them keep their vitamins.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.260
At the same time, these lobbyists

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.390
targeted the lawmakers themselves,

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.520
convincing them to oppose the legislation

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.770
that was under consideration in Congress,

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:23.460
and to actually counter it
by passing their own law,

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.410
a law that would be
friendly to the industry.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.090
And you can actually see this point blank.

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:28.329
Sometimes lobbying is foggy,

00:08:28.329 --> 00:08:29.490
and we don't know what happened,

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:33.090
but in this case the senators
who received the most money

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:35.070
from the industry were the ones

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:39.210
who actually drafted the
new bill for this law.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.353
And here it is.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:45.983
Public law 103-417 from October 25, 1994.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:50.640
So what started as an attempt
to regulate supplements

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.380
actually turned into a law

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.000
that is friendly to the industry,

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.231
and the reason we have this.

00:08:57.231 --> 00:08:59.981
(dramatic music)

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:07.290
I mean I love when you're neck
deep in one of these laws,

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:08.580
and you just see a statement

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:12.240
that just makes it so clear
who was influencing this law.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:13.073
Check this out.

00:09:13.073 --> 00:09:13.980
This law just straight up says

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.780
that the federal government should not

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.670
take any actions to impose

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:21.390
unreasonable regulatory
barriers towards this industry.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:23.078
And especially, says the law,

00:09:23.078 --> 00:09:25.830
this industry is really lucrative.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:29.130
It has annual sales of $4 billion.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.800
Congress wouldn't wanna slow that down.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.430
So then the big kicker here,

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:35.040
one of the key parts of the law is that

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.870
they specify that supplements,

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:40.401
the thing in this bottle is
not classified as medicine,

00:09:40.401 --> 00:09:42.644
it's classified as food.

00:09:42.644 --> 00:09:45.600
That's how the FDA
should treat it, as food.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.910
But supplements are not food

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:50.880
in the same way a bag of Doritos is food,

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.075
they're much more complicated.

00:09:52.075 --> 00:09:53.760
But we'll get back to that in a sec.

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:55.792
The point is that this
law gave the industry

00:09:55.792 --> 00:09:57.420
a lot of freedom,

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:59.820
including what kind of
claims they could make.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.220
The law gave them the authority
to say a lot of things

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:04.620
about what their health
supplement does for people

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.274
as long as they include
this one disclaimer.

00:10:07.274 --> 00:10:09.964
I'm looking at Genius Mushrooms.

00:10:09.964 --> 00:10:13.473
The product says that it is
healthy immune system support,

00:10:13.473 --> 00:10:15.480
energy and clarity.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:16.440
Sounds great.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:20.280
But then here on the back
in very, very, very small,

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:23.100
teeny tiny, almost illegible font,

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.520
zoom in here, you will
see a teeny tiny statement

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.280
that complies with the law.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.540
These statements have not been evaluated

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:31.620
by the food administrator.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:32.970
This product is not intended to diagnose.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:34.710
It's right there in the fine print

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:36.000
that no one is reading.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.100
What people are reading is this.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:41.130
Healthy immune system
support, energy and clarity.

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:45.030
I mean, the law is so
friendly to the industry.

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:45.984
It allows these companies

00:10:45.984 --> 00:10:48.564
to effectively regulate themselves.

00:10:48.564 --> 00:10:49.890
The law makes it clear

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.360
that it's the government's job

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.780
to go prove that something
is adulterated or wrong

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:56.670
rather than making the companies prove

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.310
that their products are safe
before they go to market.

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:00.780
I mean it's totally backwards.

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:02.490
- We do not approve them for safety

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:04.200
and effectiveness before they are sold.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:05.490
Companies are responsible

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.473
for ensuring their products are safe.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.640
- So thanks to this 1994 law

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:14.280
supplement makers were very happy

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:17.392
because now they don't have
to tell the FDA anything.

00:11:17.392 --> 00:11:20.370
They don't have to prove that
their claims are effective,

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:22.673
they just have to put a little
tiny fine print disclaimer.

00:11:22.673 --> 00:11:26.820
And the FDA has no real
enforcement regime.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.512
They only really step in in a big way

00:11:28.512 --> 00:11:32.610
after the supplement is
proven to be hurting people.

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:33.658
Any authority they do have

00:11:33.658 --> 00:11:37.170
to check on the supplements has to be done

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.790
with their shoestring budget.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:39.623
This was Congress

00:11:39.623 --> 00:11:42.420
giving the supplement
industry a blank check,

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:44.100
telling them they can do what you want,

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:44.965
we can't regulate you,

00:11:44.965 --> 00:11:46.440
it's now the law.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:49.471
And this is why the industry went from

00:11:49.471 --> 00:11:51.850
a $4 billion industry in the early 90's

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:55.741
to a $53 billion industry today.

00:11:55.741 --> 00:11:58.440
This is why Americans are now

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.940
inundated with capsules

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.130
and pills and drops and creams

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:05.910
and teas that claim to
make your body work better.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.020
But this is confusing

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:10.890
because supplements actually
do have a place in our lives

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.015
for certain people who need certain things

00:12:13.015 --> 00:12:14.580
that their body can't make.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.170
So one of my questions
going into all of this is

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:20.310
what of this is legit?

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:21.143
Is any of it,

00:12:21.143 --> 00:12:22.833
or is it all just snake oil?

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.387
What does the science actually say?

00:12:26.387 --> 00:12:28.970
(gentle music)

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.210
There's been a lot of good study on this,

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:38.905
and luckily we got one
of those amazing things

00:12:38.905 --> 00:12:41.401
where they do a study
of all of the studies,

00:12:41.401 --> 00:12:43.260
and they put it all together,

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.093
and they say

00:12:44.093 --> 00:12:45.037
"This is what all the studies

00:12:45.037 --> 00:12:46.770
"have concluded over the years."

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:49.140
Like a good old meta-analysis.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.160
This meta-analysis,

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.134
which used 84 studies,

00:12:52.134 --> 00:12:53.950
and put it all together
to find conclusions,

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.670
found that vitamins and supplements

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.471
were generally, quote,
associated with little

00:12:59.471 --> 00:13:01.895
or no benefit in preventing cancer,

00:13:01.895 --> 00:13:04.320
cardiovascular disease and death.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:05.153
It had a little bit

00:13:05.153 --> 00:13:06.990
of a benefit on treating cancer

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:07.980
if you already have it.

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:11.534
They also found that people
with a high risk of lung cancer

00:13:11.534 --> 00:13:14.880
had a, quote, increased
risk of lung cancer

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.320
and other harmful outcomes

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:18.420
by taking one vitamin, betacarotene.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.450
So what this basically is saying
is that vitamins don't work

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.920
for the big things,

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.680
preventing the killers like
cancer and heart problems.

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:28.560
And they maybe even hurt us in some cases,

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.000
depending on the supplement.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.430
But in reading these
conclusions you start to realize

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:34.440
just how complex this is.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:37.470
There are like thousands
of different supplements,

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:40.944
and there are innumerable
numbers of individual bodies

00:13:40.944 --> 00:13:44.100
that have different chemistry
and different experiences.

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:45.682
It starts to get confusing

00:13:45.682 --> 00:13:48.390
to find a satisfying conclusion.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:49.770
So we asked our experts

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:53.370
do supplements actually make
us healthier in any way?

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:55.423
- Many doctors would suggest

00:13:55.423 --> 00:13:56.730
that you don't need to
take supplements at all,

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.530
unless you have a deficiency.

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:00.750
- Ah deficiency, that's the key word here.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:03.330
So maybe my body doesn't
naturally produce enough

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:06.060
vitamin C or I don't get it in my food,

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:09.150
then a supplement would be useful.

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:10.451
- If you're a strict vegan,

00:14:10.451 --> 00:14:14.056
you have very strong dietary restrictions

00:14:14.056 --> 00:14:15.584
for whatever reason,

00:14:15.584 --> 00:14:18.120
those people probably are good candidates

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:19.770
for taking a multivitamin.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:22.320
- That's a situation where
it makes a lot of sense.

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:25.200
But most of us don't need to do that.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:26.370
Whenever there's a situation

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:28.230
where all the humans in a society

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:30.685
need a certain substance
that they're not getting,

00:14:30.685 --> 00:14:33.930
the government goes
wild to make it happen.

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:36.714
Like there was a time when we
all were deficient in iodine,

00:14:36.714 --> 00:14:39.870
so to fix this the government
worked with salt makers

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:42.150
to just put iodine in salt.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:44.220
So now all of us use it all the time,

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:45.960
and we just have enough iodine

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:48.180
because there's iodine in all of our salt.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:49.230
I guess what I'm saying here

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:51.570
is that most of us check
off all of our vitamins

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.310
and mineral needs by living

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:55.440
and eating a variety of foods.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.050
But, of course, within our
population there are people

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:00.900
who can't produce enough
of a certain vitamin,

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:03.090
or like this YouTuber

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:06.480
who just ate chicken
tenders every single day.

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:08.760
I mean they should probably
take some vitamins.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.230
You have to eat a variety of foods

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:11.850
to get all your vitamins and minerals.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:13.518
And luckily here in the 21st century

00:15:13.518 --> 00:15:17.640
we have a test to find out
how you're doing on this.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:18.525
It's a blood test.

00:15:18.525 --> 00:15:20.400
They take your blood, they test it,

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:23.970
and they find out how you're
doing on vitamins and minerals,

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:25.380
and what you might be deficient in,

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:28.170
and thus what supplements
might actually work for you.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:31.690
And yet 252 million Americans

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:36.210
are popping $53 billion worth
of supplements every year,

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:40.410
and most of them probably don't
need to be taking anything.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:41.940
Okay, so if I don't need all this,

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:45.663
but I'm taking a fistful
of vitamins every day,

00:15:45.663 --> 00:15:47.790
where does it all go?

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:50.040
- You're just peeing
out all of the excess.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:51.960
And it might give you
glow in the dark urine,

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.640
which is pretty cool,

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.640
but it's a large waste of your dollars.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:59.400
- Here's a full disclosure
that may be surprising to you.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:01.920
I take vitamins and supplements sometimes.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:05.250
I got sent this green
powder from a sponsor

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.500
who's thinking about sponsoring
a video on the channel,

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:09.240
and I totally drank it every day.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:10.560
It's a vitamin supplement.

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:12.540
It has a billion different vitamins in it.

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:15.037
And I was like "Maybe I need one of these

00:16:15.037 --> 00:16:17.197
"even though my blood
test doesn't say I do,

00:16:17.197 --> 00:16:18.397
"what if I actually do?

00:16:18.397 --> 00:16:19.800
"What if it's actually gonna help?"

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:21.213
And I tell you that to let you know

00:16:21.213 --> 00:16:22.560
that this isn't easy.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.720
This is not an easy thing to navigate.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.310
We were hit with all of these messages

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:29.887
of improve your mental
clarity, increased energy.

00:16:29.887 --> 00:16:32.670
And you're just like
"Is any of this real?"

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.980
What I'm finding is
that most of it is not.

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:37.431
But what to me is ethically wrong

00:16:37.431 --> 00:16:39.300
is when people turn to supplements

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:40.613
because they've been lied to

00:16:40.613 --> 00:16:42.600
or because they don't trust

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.000
or can't afford other forms of treatment.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.500
In other words, when they're desperate.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:48.900
- Surveys of American sentiment show

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.550
that pharmaceutical companies

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:53.031
have lower approval ratings than Congress,

00:16:53.031 --> 00:16:55.620
which is, that's pretty bad.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.870
And, again, in many ways rightly so.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.997
The profiteering off medications is,

00:17:00.997 --> 00:17:03.535
in my opinion, quite unethical.

00:17:03.535 --> 00:17:05.670
- So we hate pharmaceutical companies

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.200
for good reason, maybe,

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:10.470
but we suddenly trust
supplement companies?

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:11.701
We trust vitamins,

00:17:11.701 --> 00:17:13.740
and the industry that makes them?

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:15.720
Okay, so just quick recap.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:18.270
Supplements are the wild
west in the United States.

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:20.730
They've been very poorly regulated.

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:21.990
The industry's gone wild.

00:17:21.990 --> 00:17:23.700
They can make these wild claims.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:25.920
And a lot of us are
maybe wasting our money,

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:28.320
and peeing out supplements
that we don't need.

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:29.910
Is that the scope of the problem here,

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:31.050
just that we're wasting our money

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.940
and we're being falsely advertised to?

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.023
Doesn't seem that bad.

00:17:34.023 --> 00:17:36.900
(dramatic music)

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:39.120
That is until you realize

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:42.000
that not all supplements are harmless.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.283
The law says that supplements
should be regulated like food,

00:17:45.283 --> 00:17:47.040
but they aren't food.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:48.420
There's a lot of complicated work

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.900
that goes into creating a
high quality, safe supplement.

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:54.390
It's a complex process of manufacturing,

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:56.280
making sure that the substances are pure,

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:57.990
the dosage is correct,

00:17:57.990 --> 00:18:00.480
and it can go wrong very easily.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:03.510
- 23,000 people a year, in
fact, go to the emergency room

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:04.680
after taking a supplement.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.090
- Supplement makers don't have to prove

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:06.930
that their products are safe.

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:08.490
- It was unbelievable what we found.

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:11.340
- [Reporter] False and
unsubstantiated claims.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:14.460
- Remember L-Tryptophan back in the 80's

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:15.597
people were taking it,

00:18:15.597 --> 00:18:18.360
and they were thinking it was
gonna help with their insomnia

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.500
and helping them lose weight,

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.830
and yet it caused thousands of illnesses

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.360
and dozens of deaths.

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:25.603
One of the big problems with that

00:18:25.603 --> 00:18:29.280
was likely due to contamination
within the supplement,

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:31.380
not necessarily the substance itself.

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:33.720
A few years ago there was
a supplement that came out

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.910
that was supposed to
regulate blood circulation,

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.280
but it ended up having lead in it.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:39.960
It caused all sorts of lead poisoning,

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:41.430
and two deaths.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.360
A few years later,

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:45.780
the FDA seized 300,000 dietary supplements

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:48.720
because they had an excessive
amount of lead in them.

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:50.580
That was from one corporation.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:53.310
The FDA isn't monitoring
all of these supplements,

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:55.290
but luckily scientists are.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.090
There's this 2018 study

00:18:57.090 --> 00:19:01.555
that found that 92% of the
supplements that they studied

00:19:01.555 --> 00:19:03.302
had bacterial contamination,

00:19:03.302 --> 00:19:06.660
and 87% had fungal contamination,

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.760
which can be really
damaging for your body.

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:11.220
I'm not gonna go down a
whole literature review here

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:12.900
because there's so much of this.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:14.850
Let's just say there's a lot of instances

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:17.515
of supplements being
found to be contaminated.

00:19:17.515 --> 00:19:20.265
(dramatic music)

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:24.330
Okay, let me just tell
you one more example here

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:28.170
that is just such a good
example of the abuse

00:19:28.170 --> 00:19:29.940
of the lack of regulation here.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:31.729
There's this one plant called Kratom.

00:19:31.729 --> 00:19:34.004
I don't know, here in the
US I like feel like I see it

00:19:34.004 --> 00:19:36.060
everywhere, in every strip mall.

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:37.680
It's like Kratom Signs.

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:39.990
It's made from this evergreen tree leaf,

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:42.210
and it's sold in the form of powder

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:43.920
and pills and extracts.

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:46.050
It sounds totally natural and fresh,

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:48.900
and I can see why it's
doing so well on the market.

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:51.300
But, once again, Kratom has been linked

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:54.162
to hundreds of cases of
salmonella poisoning,

00:19:54.162 --> 00:19:56.760
and there's the fact that
it's highly addictive,

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:59.040
especially to those who
have had opioid addictions,

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.210
which is, if you haven't heard,

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:01.770
a giant problem in our country.

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:03.990
It has been deemed to
be the cause of death

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:08.990
for 91 people who had
overdoses in 2016 and 2017,

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.670
though only seven of
those people were found

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:13.320
to only have kratom in their body.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.420
There were other drugs
in the overdose as well.

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:16.830
But what we're saying here is that

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:18.360
this can be dangerous stuff.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:21.291
It's not just food like
the law wants it to be.

00:20:21.291 --> 00:20:24.120
The FDA urged the DEA to classify this

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.800
as a schedule one drug,

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:27.875
which is the classification for heroin,

00:20:27.875 --> 00:20:29.886
but it's a dietary supplement

00:20:29.886 --> 00:20:33.120
just down the road at the
local convenience store.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:36.210
Speaking of drugs, some
supplements are kind of

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.874
just like drugs in disguise.

00:20:37.874 --> 00:20:40.710
- So what we're really seeing is

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.270
that in a lot of those cases

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:44.738
they're putting in synthetic drugs,

00:20:44.738 --> 00:20:46.651
which sometimes are prescription drugs,

00:20:46.651 --> 00:20:49.037
and sometimes are products that are not

00:20:49.037 --> 00:20:50.699
approved by the FDA.

00:20:50.699 --> 00:20:54.030
- One study found that
over the last decade

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:59.030
more than 750 supplements were
illegally spiked with drugs.

00:20:59.089 --> 00:21:01.821
Only half of them were ever recalled.

00:21:01.821 --> 00:21:04.080
Wait, why can they do this?

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.990
Why can they just put
drugs, illegal drugs,

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.065
into supplements?

00:21:08.065 --> 00:21:10.075
Ah, because of this law.

00:21:10.075 --> 00:21:15.075
This law that the industry
helped pass in the 90's that says

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:18.000
that none of this has to get
any approval from the FDA.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:21.480
The FDA only steps in
when something goes wrong,

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:23.520
when the damage is already done.

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:24.750
So backwards.

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:27.060
And these companies can
get pretty aggressive.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:29.820
A few years ago, the
academics who revealed

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:31.200
that these supplement companies

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.371
were spiking their
supplements with illegal drugs

00:21:33.371 --> 00:21:36.090
got sued by one of these companies,

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:38.040
a company called
High-Tech Pharmaceuticals.

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.840
The company ended up losing the lawsuit,

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:42.090
but what it revealed is that

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:45.630
this company had been selling a product

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:49.080
that they had been ordered
to stop selling, to recall,

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:50.730
and they just never did.

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:52.980
There's so little
oversight happening here.

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:55.489
And, again, it's a giant
industry, with a lot of money

00:21:55.489 --> 00:21:57.060
and a lot of products,

00:21:57.060 --> 00:22:00.994
and it's an FDA that is very
small, with very little money,

00:22:00.994 --> 00:22:03.274
and not a lot of authority to do much.

00:22:03.274 --> 00:22:05.670
And as we mentioned at the
very beginning of the video,

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:07.050
when researchers went in

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:10.290
and just popped open some of these bottles

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:11.610
and studied the pills,

00:22:11.610 --> 00:22:13.410
they found that a lot of these supplements

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:15.960
don't actually have
what they say they have.

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:17.280
They're a totally different substance,

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:19.470
but none of us know because

00:22:19.470 --> 00:22:21.210
you don't know what calcium tastes like.

00:22:21.210 --> 00:22:22.230
- Literally there have been studies

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.730
that have shown some supplements have

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:26.153
no detectable amount of
the thing that it says

00:22:26.153 --> 00:22:27.750
is supposed to be in there.

00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:29.800
- No detectable amount.

00:22:29.800 --> 00:22:32.490
And then we've got good old melatonin.

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:34.260
I love melatonin when I need it.

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:36.637
That gummy that helps us all
get a good night's sleep.

00:22:36.637 --> 00:22:38.190
But it's not a sleeping pill, right?

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:39.632
Because it's like natural.

00:22:39.632 --> 00:22:41.760
- [Reporter] Melatonin
poisonings in children

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:44.130
have been on the rise
over the past decade.

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:46.164
- Well actually melatonin
is not a vitamin,

00:22:46.164 --> 00:22:48.881
it is a hormone that
you naturally produce.

00:22:48.881 --> 00:22:50.550
It helps induce sleep.

00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:53.069
And it's kind of been trending
over the last few years,

00:22:53.069 --> 00:22:55.320
especially among children.

00:22:55.320 --> 00:22:57.540
Over the past decade,
the number of children

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:01.770
who have overdosed on
melatonin went up 530%,

00:23:01.770 --> 00:23:03.660
causing kids to experience symptoms

00:23:03.660 --> 00:23:05.023
like vomiting and diarrhea.

00:23:05.023 --> 00:23:07.393
A lot of that is because
of dosage problems.

00:23:07.393 --> 00:23:09.210
In some cases they found

00:23:09.210 --> 00:23:13.170
that the dose is 50% higher
than what was on the label.

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:14.880
- [Reporter] The US Food
and Drug Administration

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:17.100
doesn't have any control
of the ingredients

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:19.320
or the accuracy of dosage claims.

00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:22.052
- We talked to one guy
who started a Reddit forum

00:23:22.052 --> 00:23:25.290
because he was taking Lions Mane,

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:27.186
which is a mushroom supplement,

00:23:27.186 --> 00:23:29.670
and it was causing a mysterious illness.

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:31.860
He thought it was going to give him energy

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:34.470
and mental clarity like
it says on the bottle,

00:23:34.470 --> 00:23:37.110
but instead what he experienced
was heart palpitations,

00:23:37.110 --> 00:23:38.130
sleepless nights.

00:23:38.130 --> 00:23:41.670
- I couldn't sleep for
eight months straight.

00:23:41.670 --> 00:23:44.449
By that I say one more than
one or two hours a night.

00:23:44.449 --> 00:23:45.870
- When he started the subreddit,

00:23:45.870 --> 00:23:47.760
he found thousands of others

00:23:47.760 --> 00:23:50.358
who reported a whole host
of neurological issues,

00:23:50.358 --> 00:23:54.000
chronic tension headaches,
a lack of emotion.

00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:56.112
One user's husband took his life

00:23:56.112 --> 00:23:58.050
after not being able to sleep,

00:23:58.050 --> 00:23:59.850
having constant panic attacks,

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:01.301
and losing his job over it.

00:24:01.301 --> 00:24:03.172
He was 43.

00:24:03.172 --> 00:24:06.330
- I'd been to the hospital about 20 times

00:24:06.330 --> 00:24:07.560
the first two months.

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:10.080
I have seen basically every specialist

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:11.130
that I could get ahold of,

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:13.877
and really nobody could
tell me what was going on.

00:24:13.877 --> 00:24:15.414
- These people come to Reddit

00:24:15.414 --> 00:24:18.210
because they don't have any answers.

00:24:18.210 --> 00:24:21.810
They bought a supplement
that looked legitimate,

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:23.400
promising mental clarity,

00:24:23.400 --> 00:24:24.910
and focus and energy,

00:24:24.910 --> 00:24:28.950
and had their lives completely changed.

00:24:28.950 --> 00:24:31.590
That's because our government failed.

00:24:31.590 --> 00:24:33.120
We have a government to protect us

00:24:33.120 --> 00:24:34.939
against exactly these types of things.

00:24:34.939 --> 00:24:38.010
But instead people are turning
to Reddit to find answers.

00:24:38.010 --> 00:24:41.820
To me this is the most atrocious
version of supplements.

00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:43.380
We actually reached out to the FDA

00:24:43.380 --> 00:24:46.110
as a part of this story to
understand what's the deal?

00:24:46.110 --> 00:24:47.225
Why is it like this?

00:24:47.225 --> 00:24:48.275
And they responded,

00:24:48.275 --> 00:24:50.220
and we scheduled an interview.

00:24:50.220 --> 00:24:52.290
We were gonna discuss dietary supplements

00:24:52.290 --> 00:24:53.880
and regulation in the United States,

00:24:53.880 --> 00:24:55.680
but then the day before the interview

00:24:55.680 --> 00:24:57.120
they canceled our meeting,

00:24:57.120 --> 00:24:58.833
and then just ghosted us.

00:25:00.692 --> 00:25:02.216
Luckily we have clips

00:25:02.216 --> 00:25:05.310
of former FDA commissioners
talking about this,

00:25:05.310 --> 00:25:07.579
and they all seem to agree
that this is a problem

00:25:07.579 --> 00:25:10.435
of authority and resources.

00:25:10.435 --> 00:25:13.683
- Will the FDA ever
regulate this industry?

00:25:16.170 --> 00:25:17.013
- We tried.

00:25:18.937 --> 00:25:21.520
(gentle music)

00:25:22.620 --> 00:25:24.990
- So, what can be done here?

00:25:24.990 --> 00:25:26.700
Well, luckily we live in a system

00:25:26.700 --> 00:25:29.940
where we can make change by changing laws.

00:25:29.940 --> 00:25:31.950
Like in the 90's we almost did this.

00:25:31.950 --> 00:25:35.310
If the Congress had
given the FDA more power

00:25:35.310 --> 00:25:36.870
we would have stricter punishments

00:25:36.870 --> 00:25:39.090
for supplement companies
who break the rules.

00:25:39.090 --> 00:25:41.970
We would have better rules
around what they can sell,

00:25:41.970 --> 00:25:43.495
and what claims they can make.

00:25:43.495 --> 00:25:46.410
- We should at least be able to agree

00:25:46.410 --> 00:25:48.351
that all the companies
should have to prove

00:25:48.351 --> 00:25:51.762
that they don't have bacterial
or fungal contamination,

00:25:51.762 --> 00:25:53.131
that they don't have heavy metals,

00:25:53.131 --> 00:25:55.366
that they're not containing
prescription drugs,

00:25:55.366 --> 00:25:58.029
and that they do contain the product

00:25:58.029 --> 00:26:01.590
in the dose that's specified in the pills

00:26:01.590 --> 00:26:03.210
that they're putting on their label.

00:26:03.210 --> 00:26:04.740
- I would like purity,

00:26:04.740 --> 00:26:06.060
and that people know what they're getting.

00:26:06.060 --> 00:26:07.762
I mean we owe it to
consumers at the very least

00:26:07.762 --> 00:26:09.600
that if you're gonna choose to buy it

00:26:09.600 --> 00:26:10.920
you should at least know
what you're getting.

00:26:10.920 --> 00:26:12.240
That seems like the bare minimum,

00:26:12.240 --> 00:26:13.671
and right now that's not the case.

00:26:13.671 --> 00:26:15.600
- The experts we talked to don't think

00:26:15.600 --> 00:26:17.899
that supplements should
be regulated like drugs.

00:26:17.899 --> 00:26:19.438
I think that makes sense.

00:26:19.438 --> 00:26:21.300
But they agree that we should start

00:26:21.300 --> 00:26:22.920
with giving the FDA the authority

00:26:22.920 --> 00:26:24.360
and the resources it needs

00:26:24.360 --> 00:26:28.189
to monitor supplements so we
know what's actually in them,

00:26:28.189 --> 00:26:30.755
so that we're not
trusting the honor system

00:26:30.755 --> 00:26:34.380
of for-profit companies to obey the rules,

00:26:34.380 --> 00:26:36.660
and to actually put in these supplements

00:26:36.660 --> 00:26:39.143
what they say is in these supplements.

00:26:39.143 --> 00:26:40.710
This would mean the FDA going

00:26:40.710 --> 00:26:43.050
and conducting spot checks more often

00:26:43.050 --> 00:26:45.000
and more aggressively to make sure

00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:46.740
that this stuff is correct,

00:26:46.740 --> 00:26:49.740
and that it's being
manufactured in a clean way,

00:26:49.740 --> 00:26:51.000
free of contamination.

00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:52.800
Congress has recently considered a bill

00:26:52.800 --> 00:26:53.910
that would help with this,

00:26:53.910 --> 00:26:55.650
including trying to create a database

00:26:55.650 --> 00:26:56.760
of all the supplements

00:26:56.760 --> 00:26:59.550
so that the FDA at least
knows what's on the market.

00:26:59.550 --> 00:27:01.552
But, of course, the supplement
lobby's not gonna stand back.

00:27:01.552 --> 00:27:04.620
They spend over $2 million
a year on lobbying,

00:27:04.620 --> 00:27:07.620
making sure that things
stay the way they are.

00:27:07.620 --> 00:27:09.090
They make a lot of money off it.

00:27:09.090 --> 00:27:11.186
So, if you are one of the many millions

00:27:11.186 --> 00:27:13.320
who take a bunch of supplements,

00:27:13.320 --> 00:27:15.683
and are not sure if they're
spiked with weird stuff,

00:27:15.683 --> 00:27:18.812
or if you even need them, what do you do?

00:27:18.812 --> 00:27:21.577
And the answer is go
get your blood tested,

00:27:21.577 --> 00:27:24.090
and just see if you're
deficient in anything,

00:27:24.090 --> 00:27:26.310
if you actually need a dietary supplement.

00:27:26.310 --> 00:27:27.810
And even if your blood test comes back

00:27:27.810 --> 00:27:28.897
and you don't need anything,

00:27:28.897 --> 00:27:30.930
I believe that people should be able

00:27:30.930 --> 00:27:33.300
to consume whatever they want,

00:27:33.300 --> 00:27:35.370
even if it's not scientifically proven.

00:27:35.370 --> 00:27:37.830
You know your body, you
should be able to take

00:27:37.830 --> 00:27:40.953
whatever vitamin or mineral
you feel is working for you.

00:27:42.047 --> 00:27:43.481
I just think that when you
have a for-profit industry

00:27:43.481 --> 00:27:46.140
that is free to mislead and deceive

00:27:46.140 --> 00:27:47.790
and prey on consumers,

00:27:47.790 --> 00:27:49.980
you get a bunch of bad situations

00:27:49.980 --> 00:27:51.420
like the ones we've talked about here.

00:27:51.420 --> 00:27:53.010
So until the government steps in

00:27:53.010 --> 00:27:54.420
to help us navigate this,

00:27:54.420 --> 00:27:56.100
we're kind of on our own.

00:27:56.100 --> 00:27:57.930
I'm gonna put some
links in the description

00:27:57.930 --> 00:27:59.880
to third party websites that you can go to

00:27:59.880 --> 00:28:01.980
to look up your supplements,

00:28:01.980 --> 00:28:03.270
the specific supplements,

00:28:03.270 --> 00:28:06.180
and see if they've passed
a high quality standard

00:28:06.180 --> 00:28:08.100
to know if at least you're getting

00:28:08.100 --> 00:28:09.510
what it says on the bottle.

00:28:09.510 --> 00:28:12.600
So that's where we're at with supplements.

00:28:12.600 --> 00:28:14.851
We're here waiting for
transparency and accountability,

00:28:14.851 --> 00:28:17.760
and above all waiting for the regard

00:28:17.760 --> 00:28:20.700
of others' wellbeing over
the interests of an industry

00:28:20.700 --> 00:28:24.724
that seems to care more about
profit than about our health.

00:28:24.724 --> 00:28:27.307
